  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "2adb6164-9741-4da0-80de-045d7da65eb2",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Java 14 Changes\n\n## Language Changes\n\n### Finalized\n\n- Switch Expression\n\n    - Switch becomes an expression that returns a value. Supports arrow labels (no fall-through) and the yield keyword. Graduated from preview (Java 12–13) to permanent.\n\n### Preview\n\n- Pattern Matching\n    \n    - Binds a pattern variable in a single expression, eliminating the explicit cast that follows every instanceof check. \n    - The variable is in scope only where the condition is true.\n\n```sh\n    # Must enable preview features to compile\n    javac --enable-preview --release 14 MyClass.java\n\n    # And at runtime\n    java  --enable-preview MyClass\n```\n\n- Records\n\n    - Concise syntax for immutable data carrier classes.\n    - The compiler auto-generates a canonical constructor, private final fields, accessors, equals(), hashCode(), and toString().\n\n- Text Blocks\n\n    - Multi-line string literals delimited by triple quotes. \n    - Re-indentation and escape processing happen at compile time.\n    - Two new escape sequences added in this second preview.\n    \n## Platform changes\n\n### Standard\n\n- Helpful Null Pointer Exceptions\n\n    - The JVM generates a precise message describing which variable was null.\n    - Enabled by default.\n    - Eliminates the need to add debug prints to locate null in chained expressions.\n\n```sh\n    # Enabled by default in Java 14.\n    # To explicitly control it:\n\n    # Enable (default)\n    java -XX:+ShowCodeDetailsInExceptionMessages MyApp\n\n    # Disable (if you have a concern about verbose output)\n    java -XX:-ShowCodeDetailsInExceptionMessages MyApp\n\n```\n\n- JFR Event Streaming\n\n    - Java Flight Recorder data exposed as a real-time stream via `jdk.jfr.consumer.RecordingStream`.\n    - No need to dump a .jfr file and parse it separately.\n\n```java\n\n    import jdk.jfr.consumer.RecordingStream;\n\n    try (var rs = new RecordingStream()) {\n        rs.enable(\"jdk.CPULoad\").withPeriod(Duration.ofSeconds(1));\n        rs.enable(\"jdk.GarbageCollection\");\n\n        rs.onEvent(\"jdk.CPULoad\", event -> {\n            System.out.printf(\"CPU: %.1f%%%n\",\n                event.getFloat(\"machineTotal\") * 100);\n        });\n\n        rs.onEvent(\"jdk.GarbageCollection\", event -> {\n            System.out.println(\"GC cause: \" + event.getString(\"cause\"));\n        });\n\n        rs.startAsync();   // non-blocking\n        Thread.sleep(30_000);\n    }\n```\n\n\n- [NUMA](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-uniform_memory_access)-Aware memory for G1s \n\n    - G1 GC allocates young-generation regions on the NUMA node local to the allocating thread, reducing cross-node memory latency on multi-socket servers.\n\n```sh\n\n    # Enable NUMA-aware allocation for G1\n    java -XX:+UseG1GC \\\n        -XX:+UseNUMA \\\n        -Xms4g -Xmx4g \\\n        MyApp\n\n    # Verify NUMA topology at startup\n    java -XX:+UseG1GC \\\n        -XX:+UseNUMA \\\n        -Xlog:gc+heap+numa=debug \\\n        MyApp\n\n    # Output sample:\n    # [debug][gc,heap,numa] NUMA support enabled, 2 nodes detected\n\n```\n\n- ZGC on macOS and Windows\n\n    - MAC OS\n```sh\n\n    # Use ZGC on macOS (Java 14+)\n    java -XX:+UseZGC \\\n        -Xms512m -Xmx8g \\\n        MyApp\n\n    # Tune soft max heap (ZGC returns memory to OS)\n    java -XX:+UseZGC \\\n        -Xms256m -Xmx8g \\\n        -XX:SoftMaxHeapSize=2g \\\n        MyApp\n\n    # Log ZGC pauses\n    java -XX:+UseZGC \\\n        -Xlog:gc*:gc.log:time,uptime \\\n        MyApp\n\n```\n\n    - Windows OS\n\n```sh\n    # Enable ZGC on Windows (same flags as Linux/macOS)\n    java -XX:+UseZGC -Xmx4g MyApp\n\n    # ZGC on Windows requires:\n    #   Windows 10 / Server 2019 or later\n    #   JDK 14+ 64-bit\n\n    # Confirm ZGC is active in GC log\n    java -XX:+UseZGC \\\n        -Xlog:gc::time \\\n        MyApp\n    # Output: [2024-...] Using ZGC\n```\n\n- Non-Volatile Memory Byte Buffers\n\n    - New FileChannel.MapMode constants (READ_ONLY_SYNC, READ_WRITE_SYNC) create MappedByteBuffer instances over persistent/non-volatile memory (NVM/PMEM), with synchronous flush semantics.\n\n```java\n\n    import java.nio.channels.FileChannel;\n    import java.nio.file.*;\n    import jdk.nio.mapmode.ExtendedMapMode;\n\n    Path pmemFile = Path.of(\"/mnt/pmem/data.bin\");\n\n    try (FileChannel fc = FileChannel.open(\n            pmemFile, StandardOpenOption.READ, StandardOpenOption.WRITE)) {\n\n        // READ_WRITE_SYNC: writes go directly to persistent memory\n        var buf = fc.map(ExtendedMapMode.READ_WRITE_SYNC, 0, 4096);\n\n        buf.putInt(0, 0xDEADBEEF);\n        // No explicit force() needed — data is durable immediately\n    }\n```\n\n### Incubator\n\n- jpackage (Packaging Tool)\n\n    - Bundles a Java application into a self-contained native installer. Produces .exe / .msi on Windows, .dmg / .pkg on macOS, .deb / .rpm on Linux.\n\n```sh\n    # Package a modular application (produces platform-native installer)\njpackage \\\n--name       MyApp \\\n--module-path mods \\\n--module      com.example.myapp/com.example.myapp.Main \\\n--type        dmg          # dmg | pkg | exe | msi | deb | rpm\n\n# Package a non-modular jar\njpackage \\\n--name        MyApp \\\n--input       lib \\\n--main-jar    myapp.jar \\\n--main-class  com.example.Main \\\n--type        exe\n\n# Custom icon and version\njpackage \\\n--name    MyApp \\\n--input   lib \\\n--main-jar myapp.jar \\\n--icon    resources/icon.ico \\\n--app-version 1.0.0\n```\n\n### Removed\n\n- CMS GC Removal\n    - The Concurrent Mark Sweep garbage collector is fully removed. Deprecated in Java 9. Migrate to G1 (default) or ZGC / Shenandoah for low-latency requirements.\n\n```sh\n\n    # Java 13 and earlier (deprecated)\n    java -XX:+UseConcMarkSweepGC MyApp\n    # Warning: ConcMarkSweepGC is deprecated...\n\n    # Java 14 — using CMS is an error\n    java -XX:+UseConcMarkSweepGC MyApp\n    # Error: VM option 'UseConcMarkSweepGC' is obsolete...\n\n    # ✅ Migrate to G1 (default since Java 9)\n    java -XX:+UseG1GC MyApp\n\n    # ✅ Or ZGC for low-latency workloads\n    java -XX:+UseZGC MyApp\n\n    # ✅ Or Shenandoah (available in some distributions)\n    java -XX:+UseShenandoahGC MyApp\n```\n\n- ParallelScavenge & SerialOldGC Combo deprecated \n\n    - The rarely-used combination of Parallel young-gen GC with Serial old-gen GC is deprecated. Almost no production systems use this pairing.\n\n```sh\n\n    # Deprecated combination (triggers warning in Java 14)\n    java -XX:+UseParallelGC -XX:-UseParallelOldGC MyApp\n    # Warning: deprecated combination, consider migrating\n\n    # ✅ Standard Parallel GC (uses ParallelOldGC by default)\n    java -XX:+UseParallelGC MyApp\n\n    # ✅ Or switch to G1\n    java -XX:+UseG1GC MyApp\n```",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "2adb6164-9741-4da0-80de-045d7da65eb2"
      }
    },
